    "summary": "UNCONFIRMED violator. What IS confirmed from verbatim source is the contract the violating update path must be brought in line with, and it is owned in two repositories that do not import one another. tldraw/packages/store/src/lib/IncrementalSetConstructor.ts:25-102 holds the additive-and-subtractive half: private _add records into this.diff.added (lines 91-102) and the remove path records into this.diff.removed, while get() at lines 71-82 returns { value: this.nextValue!, diff: this.diff! } \u2014 the builder tracks both directions as it goes and can still yield the whole set. react/packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactChildFiber.js holds the rendered half: after walking the new children slot by slot it reaches lines 1266-1268, '// We've reached the end of the new children. We can delete the rest.' -> deleteRemainingChildren(returnFiber, oldFiber), with the same drop applied at :1770 and :2031 \u2014 a keyed pass that removes the children whose keys are gone. Candidate violators were opened and all RULED OUT against source because each converges: jotai/src/vanilla/utils/splitAtom.ts:64-136 rebuilds atomList/keyList from scratch each pass; tldraw/packages/editor/src/lib/editor/derivations/parentsToChildren.ts:94-110 splices removed shapes and then compacts with arr.length = writeIdx; xyflow/packages/system/src/utils/store.ts:143-144 calls nodeLookup.clear(); parentLookup.clear() before re-adopting; db/packages/vue-db/src/useLiveQuery.ts:362-363 does internalData.length = 0 then push(...), db/packages/svelte-db/src/useLiveQuery.svelte.ts:380-381 reassigns internalData = [] then pushes, db/packages/solid-db/src/useLiveQuery.ts:348-350 uses reconcile(Array.from(...)), db/packages/react-db/src/useLiveQuery.ts:525-542 rebuilds data from a captured entries array; query/packages/vue-query/src/useQueries.ts:346 replaces state.value wholesale, query/packages/solid-query/src/useQueries.ts:232-244 resets the whole store on queries.length change, and query/package